seg-4c412bb0ce63 = Every run of the command-line interface (CLI) writes a report beside its result: a printable HyperText Markup Language (HTML) page, <c1/>, and a machine-readable JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) document, <c2/>, with the same content. The report works for any scenario kind and for campaigns.

# text
seg-e26b1a83a86d = The result document answers <em>what the engine computed</em>. The report adds what a reader needs before acting on it: what went in, what the numbers rest on, what was left out, and how to get the same bytes again. It invents none of that. Every section is read from a source the engine already keeps, and names the source beside what it quotes.

# text
# c1: kshana::advanced_report
# c2: src/advanced_report.rs
seg-bf0456f18e4f = The builder is <c1/> (<c2/>). It is a pure function of the run output, the scenario file's bytes and the command line: it reads no clock, no file and no network, and it builds for WebAssembly.

