# c7: spectrum
# c8: [[panels]]
# c9: leo-pass
# c10: leo-pnt-chain
# c11: leo-navmsg
# c12: leo-pvt
# c13: terrain-nav
# c14: terrain-slam
seg-f38434695c28 = A row that grades only one input path of a kind is listed only when the run took that path (<c1/>): <c2/> and <c3/> carry the "Orbit propagation & determination" row only with a <c4/> (the Simplified General Perturbations { "4" } (SGP4) path; an analytic orbit is a two-body propagation), and <c5/> carries the measured-record row only with an <c6/>. The same table gates the <c7/> multi-band row on the run drawing <c8/>, and the rows of the low Earth orbit (LEO) kinds on the path each run took: a <c9/> or <c10/> rain, building-entry, low-energy or spoofer row only when the scenario sets that term, the scintillation row unless the scenario switches it off, a <c11/>, <c12/> or chain precise-point-positioning row only for the analysis or mode the result carries, and the LEO system-preset row only when a named preset is used. The Shuttle Radar Topography Mission (SRTM) reader row is carried by no kind: <c13/> and <c14/> run on a synthetic digital elevation model (DEM), and no scenario field reads an SRTM tile. A VALIDATED row the run never touched would otherwise claim evidence the run does not have.

