seg-8a3fc60a5b54 = Printing to PDF

# text
# c1: --report pdf
# c2: report.html
seg-201bcec2caa3 = The engine does not write Portable Document Format (PDF) files. A PDF writer that renders the charts would mean a new, heavy dependency, so there is no <c1/> option. Instead, <c2/> carries a print stylesheet: open it in a browser, print, and choose "Save as PDF".

# text
seg-13f1f294ede1 = The stylesheet is written for both A4 and US Letter. It sets no paper size (the print dialog's choice applies), keeps { "15" } mm / { "14" } mm margins that fit either sheet, switches to black on white, repeats table headers on every page, keeps table rows, figures and cards from splitting across pages, keeps headings with the text that follows, and starts the inputs, results, verification-labels and reproducibility sections on a new page. The navigation bar is hidden in print.

